  "verbalization": "Phyllofolactones F appears to be a target of multiple compounds that ultimately lead to NH-6 through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Phyllofolactones F interacts with T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, which is then targeted by 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, both of which have NH-6 as their target. This indicates a potential pathway where Phyllofolactones F is indirectly linked to NH-6 through the action of these compounds. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Phyllofolactones F serves as a receptor or binding site for these secondary compounds, which in turn interact with NH-6. The integration of these paths highlights a possible dependency on these secondary molecules, suggesting that Phyllofolactones F may be involved in a broader network of interactions that ultimately affect NH-6.",
